    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-12",
      "edition": "Thursday 12 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Galthié recalls Alldritt at No. 8 after almost a year out",
          "body": "Grégory Alldritt returns to the starting side for Friday's clash with South Africa, wearing the No. 8 shirt after almost a year out of favour with head coach Fabien Galthié. Galthié has picked him to counter the Springboks' forward power, and the La Rochelle forward was left out of this year's Six Nations. Planet Rugby's winners-and-losers verdict on the team names Maxime Lucu a winner, back at scrum-half with Antoine Dupont moving to fly-half. Romain Ntamack, Matthieu Jalibert and Thomas Ramos are all out injured, leaving Lucu with the nine shirt."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Argentina captain Julián Montoya out of Italy test after HIA",
          "body": "All Blacks' Will Jordan doubtful for Wales with suspected hamstring injury. Wales's Taine Basham poised for back row against All Blacks."
