      }
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-12",
      "edition": "Thursday 12 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection bid",
          "heading": "Joey Carbery bids for Ireland's No. 10 shirt after missing Farrell's squad",
          "body": "The Leinster fly-half wants the Test number 10 jersey, telling the Ireland Rugby Social, \"It's what I want.\" Carbery, who won the last of his 37 caps against Fiji in November 2022, has made just two starts since rejoining Leinster from Bordeaux-Begles. He missed Ireland head coach Andy Farrell's latest squad, but has been included in Mark Sexton's Ireland XV panel for next week's match against Fiji 'A' in Cork. He calls it \"a foot back in the door of the Irish system and the way they play.\""
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France recall Alldritt at No. 8 after almost a year out",
