    "389": {
      "date": "2026-11-12",
      "edition": "Thursday 12 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection outlook",
          "heading": "Diego Dominguez calls Italy timid against South Africa, hopes to see Allan",
          "body": "Former Italy and Argentina fly-half Diego Dominguez, now a Sky Sport pitchside pundit, judged Italy timid, especially in the first half, after the 7-66 defeat to South Africa. He said the Springboks could put 40-50 points on anyone, and Italy were limited to watching their opponents. Dominguez thinks prop Danilo Fischetti and back-rower Ross Vintcent could find a place straight away against Argentina, and hopes to see fly-half Tommaso Allan, whose kicking he rates as the best in the squad."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France recall Alldritt at No. 8 after almost a year out",
