      "edition": "Thursday 12 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching succession",
          "heading": "RUCK's hypothetical odds put Ronan O'Gara among Gregor Townsend's 10 possible successors",
          "body": "RUCK has ranked 10 candidates to succeed Scotland head coach Gregor Townsend, whose contract runs to the end of the 2027 Rugby World Cup. These are hypothetical odds rather than bookmaker prices, and no official shortlist has been announced. Ronan O'Gara, the former Ireland fly-half, is the 33/1 outsider, but he extended his La Rochelle contract to 2031 in September and there is no indication he is pursuing the job. Former Scotland lock Jim Hamilton has also thrown his support behind Mike Blair."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
