          "body": "Former Springboks lock Mark Andrews, a 1995 World Cup winner, told the Big Men Talking podcast that head coach Rassie Erasmus picked Siya Kolisi as captain because \"he was the best captain that he had\". Andrews recalled Kolisi's humility at a jersey handover, when the young skipper showed real respect for an older player. Kolisi has since led the Boks to 58 Test wins, the most by any Springboks captain, after passing John Smit's 54 earlier this year."
